        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Bakes a user-chosen adjustment into the JPEG at <emphasis>path</emphasis>, letting the user manually correct a photo before saving. Unlike the orientation compensation, this applies on all platforms. <emphasis>rotation</emphasis> is a clockwise angle in degrees (any multiple of 90) and <emphasis>mirror</emphasis> applies a horizontal flip. The mirror is applied before the rotation to match the live preview.</para>
<para>Returns false without touching the file when there is nothing to apply (zero rotation and no mirror). </para>
